(project pricklypear-film-analysis
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: film analysis — shot/scene structure, chiastic (ring) analysis, cut comparison as branches")
 (status planned)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section film-analysis

  (doc "Films as queryable structure: scenes with frame-exact timecodes,
        motifs and beats, chiastic analysis over scene rings, and
        alternate cuts as branches. Analysis is data on the image;
        media files never are.")
  (status planned)
  (verify
   (build "dune build image")
   (smoke "(load-library \"film\") installs film/… bindings and routes")
   (smoke "create a film, ingest scenes, run film/report over a branch")
   (smoke "GET /film lists films; /film/<slug> shows ring report")
   (smoke "pp_eval film/… entry points work for agents"))

  (details
   (doc (|
        =========================================================
        PRODUCT INTENT
        =========================================================
        A first-class film-analysis workbench on the live image.

        The motivating observation: long-form narratives carry
        structural meaning in temporal placement — chiastic (ring)
        composition where scene k mirrors scene n-k+1, a "mirror
        moment" at the temporal center, timed plant/payoff pairs.
        This structure is *checkable*, not just interpretable — but
        no NLE or spreadsheet treats a cut as queryable, branchable
        data. Pricklypear does.

        Three workloads, one substrate:
          1. ANALYSIS  — structure of published films (the Shining
             European-vs-US cut comparison is the first corpus).
             Machine-detected scene boundaries as ground truth on
             one branch; human curation as a fork.
          2. LINTING   — report unpaired mirrors, orphan plants,
             per-pair duration deltas, a whole-cut tightness score.
             The chiastic claim becomes a number.
          3. AUTHORING — later, the same machinery pointed at one's
             own footage: dailies auto-split, motifs tracked, the
             cut linted before render.

        Domain tension (the whole design):
          - The interesting claims are EXACT (frame-exact pairing,
            center-scene identity, tightness scores).
          - The interesting readings are FLUID (this scene mirrors
            that one; this beat pays off that plant).

        Resolution: scenes/motifs/beats as boring typed rows;
        chiastic truth DERIVED from position, never stored; human
        declarations kept as separate fields so the linter can
        report where declaration and derivation disagree — that
        disagreement is the analysis.

        Inspired by:
          - ring composition scholarship (Mary Douglas et al.)
          - craft literature (mirror-moment midpoint, timed beats)
          - quantitative film studies (Cinemetrics-style shot data)
          - the corkboard: cards, colored by thread, moved by hand

        NOT a video editor. NOT a media store (no frames, no clips —
        media stays on the laptop; the image holds only structure
        and metadata). NOT a generation pipeline (AI video gen is a
        separate future chapter gated on an http prim). NOT a
        platform for redistributing copyrighted media — the
        PUBLISHABLE artifact is analysis (numbers, reports, essays),
        never footage.

        Killer property: a cut is a branch. The US cut and the
        European cut of the same film are sibling branches over
        shared film rows; "the recut tightened the ring" is a diff
        of two generated reports.

        =========================================================
        LAYERING
        =========================================================
        - libs/film/lib.pp      — package film/… (seed on system/main)
        - data_rows types       — film, scene, motif, beat
        - Routes via (route …)  — /film and report paths
        - scripts/film_ingest   — laptop-side extraction → Nopales
                                  source → pp_eval (see ingestion)
        - OCaml                 — existing CRUD/list/dict prims only;
                                  NO new kernel prims required for v1

        Analysis functions are PURE Nopales over (rows …) results:
        chiasm/pairs walks a sorted scene list two-pointer style;
        chiasm/center is the same recursion returning the singleton
        remainder (odd-length ring) or empty (even-length ring has a
        center SEAM, not a center scene — both shapes reported).

        =========================================================
        DATA MODEL (v1)
        =========================================================
        Types (deftype on load). Timecodes are INTEGER FRAME COUNTS;
        fps lives on the film row; seconds are a rendering concern.

        film
          slug            string  ; "the-shining"
          title           string
          year            string
          fps             string number  ; "23.976" | "24" | "25"
          notes           string

        scene   ; ONE detected/curated scene in ONE cut
          film            string  ; film slug
          cut             string  ; cut label, e.g. "eu" | "us" | "auto-t12"
          ord             string int  ; position in THIS cut
          slug            string  ; "room237" ("" until curated)
          summary         string
          tc_in           string int  ; frames
          dur             string int  ; frames
          mirror          string  ; DECLARED mirror scene slug or ""
                                  ; derivation from ord is the truth;
                                  ; this field is a claim to check

        motif   ; a tracked recurrence
          film            string
          name            string  ; "mirror" | "red-key" | …
          kind            string  ; prop | line | color | sound | image

        beat    ; a motif occurrence inside a scene
          scene           string  ; scene id
          motif           string  ; motif name
          role            string  ; plant | payoff | echo
          tc              string int  ; frames, absolute

        Why frames-as-strings: data_rows fields are strings; integer
        frames avoid float rounding across fps conversions. "To the
        second" claims are rendered, not stored.

        NO shot-level table in v1 (shots matter for production, not
        for ring analysis; a shot type is a later subsection if the
        authoring workload arrives).
         NO extra per-type user ACL — the RLS floor already scopes rows to
         their author (data.u.<user>.*); isolation is not per-branch.
        NO media blobs, thumbnails, or waveforms. Ever. Paths/hashes
        in notes fields at most.

        =========================================================
        CHIASM AS DERIVATION (the core idea)
        =========================================================
        The pairing is positional: in a ring of n scenes, scene k
        mirrors scene n-k+1. Therefore:

          (chiasm/pairs scenes)   ; two-pointer recursion: pair ends,
                                  ; recurse inward → list of pairs
          (chiasm/center scenes)  ; same recursion; odd ring leaves
                                  ; the CENTER SCENE as a singleton;
                                  ; even ring returns '() (center is
                                  ; the seam between the middle pair)

        The mirror scene falls out of the structure. Nobody
        annotates it; the report NAMES it.

        Report shape (film/report scenes) — a dict/assoc tree:
          center     center scene or center seam
          shape      odd | even
          pairs      per-pair: slugs, dur delta (frames), shared motifs
          declared   declared-mirror mismatches (claim vs position)
          orphans    plant beats with no downstream payoff beat
          tightness  sum of per-pair dur deltas (lower = tighter ring)

        The linter's most interesting output is DISAGREEMENT:
          - declared mirror ≠ derived mirror → either the annotation
            is wrong or the film breaks its own ring deliberately
            (broken symmetry is itself a finding)
          - derived pair with strong shared motifs but no declared
            mirror → an unnoticed mirror, proposed by the machine

        =========================================================
        INGESTION (laptop-side, no new kernel prims)
        =========================================================
        Scene boundaries come from the media file ON THE LAPTOP,
        never from the image:

          ffmpeg -i cut.mp4 -an -vf "scdet=threshold=N,showinfo" \
            -f null -   → cut log with pts_time per detected cut

        scripts/film_ingest (ksh) parses the log and EMITS Nopales
        source — (film/scene-create …) forms — piped to pp_eval
        over the existing /api/eval endpoint. The image receives
        already-structured data through the normal eval path.

        Known detector limits (documented, accepted):
          - scdet finds CUTS, not narrative scenes: dissolves, long
            fades, and match cuts slip or merge; threshold is
            per-film tuning. Adjacent detections are merged by hand
            during curation — this is expected work, not failure.
          - Detection lands on a MACHINE branch (e.g. cut label
            "auto-t12"); curation happens on a fork so ground truth
            stays pure and detector re-runs are diffable.

        Optional later sources through the SAME emitter path:
          - whisper.cpp transcripts → dialogue beats with timestamps
          - PySceneDetect XML/EDL export instead of raw ffmpeg logs
          - frame-similarity pass (pHash / ffmpeg signature) →
            PROPOSED mirror pairs (machine seeds, human accepts)

        =========================================================
        CUTS AS BRANCHES
        =========================================================
        Branch convention (per habitat-workflow session ritual):
          analysis/<film>/<cut>-auto      machine ground truth
          analysis/<film>/<cut>-curated   fork; slugs, mirrors, beats

        Cut comparison = run film/report per branch, diff the trees.
        "The recut tightened the ring" becomes: tightness(eu) <
        tightness(us), with the per-pair table behind it.

        =========================================================
        PUBLISHING BOUNDARY
        =========================================================
        Personal analysis of owned media for criticism is the
        intended use. What MAY be published from the habitat:
        reports, numbers, essays, generated diagrams. What MUST NOT
        be: footage, frames, audio, or anything that reconstructs
        the work. No public routes serve derived media; report
        routes are private by default.
    |)))

  (subsection model
   (doc "film/scene/motif/beat types; integer-frame timecodes; declared-vs-derived mirror split")
   (status planned)
   (verify
    (smoke "load-library defines film, scene, motif, beat types")
    (smoke "scene-create stores cut/ord/tc_in/dur as frame integers")
    (smoke "mirror field is a declaration; derivation comes from ord")
    (smoke "fps lives on film; seconds are render-only")))

  (subsection ingestion
   (doc "laptop-side scdet/ffmpeg → Nopales emitter → pp_eval; machine branch stays pure, curation is a fork")
   (status planned)
   (verify
    (smoke "scripts/film_ingest parses an scdet log into scene-create forms")
    (smoke "ingesting a short clip creates ordered scenes on an -auto branch")
    (smoke "re-ingest at a new threshold lands on a new cut label, old branch untouched")))

  (subsection chiastic-analysis
   (doc "chiasm/pairs + chiasm/center two-pointer derivation; film/report with pairs, declared mismatches, orphan plants, tightness")
   (status planned)
   (verify
    (smoke "chiasm/pairs on a known list returns end-paired list")
    (smoke "chiasm/center returns singleton on odd ring, empty on even")
    (smoke "film/report names the center scene from structure alone")
    (smoke "declared mirror mismatch appears in report.declared")
    (smoke "orphan plant (no downstream payoff) appears in report.orphans")
    (smoke "tightness is the sum of per-pair dur deltas")))

  (subsection cut-comparison
   (doc "cuts as branches; report-per-branch diff answers 'did the recut tighten the ring'")
   (status planned)
   (verify
    (smoke "two cut labels over one film produce independent reports")
    (smoke "tightness diff between cuts is computable via pp_eval")))

  (subsection ui
   (doc "routes /film, /film/<slug>; ring report page with per-pair table and rainbow-style arc diagram via render-html")
   (status planned)
   (verify
    (smoke "GET /film 200 after load-library")
    (smoke "GET /film/<slug> renders center, pairs table, tightness")
    (smoke "diagram renders arcs between derived mirror pairs")))

  (subsection agent-access
   (doc "pp_eval film/… as the API; reports are data trees an agent can diff")
   (status planned)
   (verify
    (smoke "pp_eval film/report returns the full report tree")
    (smoke "pp_eval scene/beats queries work per film and cut")))
 )
)
